DISCLAIMER (not part of the MIT License terms above; it neither adds to nor
restricts the permissions granted, and is stated here so that it travels with
the code)

This software automates the *building* of geotechnical models. It does not
perform, replace, or verify engineering judgement.

The Software constructs geometry, materials, structural elements and
calculation phases exactly as the parameter files describe them, including
whatever is erroneous in them. It does not check that a model is physically
sensible, that material parameters are appropriate for the ground being
modelled, that the idealisation suits the problem, or that any computed result
is meaningful. Numerical output produced with the help of this Software is not
a design, a recommendation, or a certification of safety or fitness.

Any model built with this Software, and any result derived from it, must be
independently reviewed and approved by a qualified geotechnical engineer
competent in the relevant jurisdiction before it is used for, or relied upon
in, the design, assessment, or construction of anything. Responsibility for
that review, and for any use of the results, rests entirely with the user.

